<h3>Unit reading</h3>
<p>This unit has one text: <em>Existentialism Is a Humanism</em>, a lecture Sartre delivered in Paris in 1945 and published the following year. It is the shortest primary text in the course — about 25–30 pages depending on the translation — and one of the most re-readable. Plan to read it twice: once to get the shape of the argument, once to press on the details.</p>
<h4>Primary text</h4>
<div>
<p>Jean-Paul Sartre, <em>Existentialism Is a Humanism</em> (1946)</p>
<p>Trans. Carol Macomber (Yale University Press, 2007) is the preferred translation. The older Philip Mairet translation is available free online and is acceptable for reading.</p>
<p>→ Read the full text online: <a href="https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/sartre/works/exist/sartre.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>Existentialism Is a Humanism</em></a></p>
</div>
