<p>△ Note on the text</p>
<p>Sartre later said he was not entirely happy with this lecture — he thought it oversimplified some of his positions and that parts of it were misunderstood by his audience. Read it knowing that it is a public-facing summary, not the full technical argument of <em>Being and Nothingness</em>. For our purposes, it is the right entry point: the ideas are here, clearly stated, and the text is short enough to read with real attention.</p>
</div></div>
